<title>USA: Weekend box office chart -- Sept 27-29.</title>
<headline>Weekend box office chart -- Sept 27-29.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the September 27-29 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross   Cumulative gross</p>
<p>1. First Wives Club	$15,314,530	$ 41,784,740</p>
<p>2. Extreme Measures	 $6,906,546	   ---</p>
<p>3. Last Man Standing	$3,577,922	$ 12,696,135</p>
<p>4. 2 Days in the Valley   $3,352,440	$  ----</p>
<p>5. Fly Away Home	    $3,004,901	$ 13,327,850</p>
<p>6. Independence Day	 $2,550,338	$293,617,050</p>
<p>7. Bulletproof		$1,946,905	$ 18,403,880</p>
<p>8. First Kid		  $1,847,745	$ 22,486,285</p>
<p>9. Maximum Risk	     $1,602,428	$ 12,777,649</p>
<p>10 Tin Cup		    $1,153,856	$ 51,272,932</p>
<p>NOTE: First Wives Club is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc. &quot;Extreme Measures&quot;, &quot;Fly Away Home&quot; and &quot;Maximum Risk&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp. &quot;Last Man Standing&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Turner Broadcasting System Inc . 2 Days in the Valley is released by MGM, which is being bought by a consortium backed by investor Kirk Kerkorian. &quot;Independence Day&quot; is released by News Corp's 20th Century Fox. &quot;Bulletproof&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co Ltd. &quot;First Kid&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Tin Cup&quot; is released by Time Warner Inc's Warner Bros.</p>
